<<~ ahu slot=`#/bearing`>>
! Artifact Contract

Keep the artistic invitation, artifact requirements, and actual execution record distinct. Use this companion only when output properties need to be checked or enforced. Do not add new `art()` parameters.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/registers`>>
!! Keep three records

* `Art Sigil` — the intended worktype, read, imagery, treatment, composition, relation and depiction-scope.
* `Artifact contract` — required output category, dimensions, support, channels, alignment, color space, exact text, file structure and delivery conditions, as applicable. Mark requirements `mandatory`, `preferred`, `delegated` or `unset`.
* `Execution record` — actual receiver, accessible inputs, transformations, measurements, produced outputs, failed checks and accepted deviations.

Do not treat a technically valid file as evidence of artistic success, or an attractive image as proof of technical compliance.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/transparency`>>
!! Distinguish transparency properties

* `Artistic translucency` — represented or simulated light transmission.
* `Pixel alpha` — channel values in a delivered file; visible translucency does not guarantee an alpha channel.
* `Layer opacity` — attenuation of a source layer during composition, distinct from the source pixel alpha.

Where a property is mandatory, inspect the delivered file or use an appropriate deterministic operation. A language instruction is not a validation result.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/card`>>
!! Minimal contract

```toml
[artifact]
role = "transparent overlay"
format = "PNG/RGBA"
canvas_px = [512, 512]
alpha = "clear margins required to have alpha 0"
registration = "specified base canvas origin"
preserve_source = true

[execution]
receiver = "record actual receiver"
inputs = "record verified access"
checks = ["dimensions", "alpha", "composite at intended scale"]
results = "record observations and deviations"
acceptance = "operator decision"
```

This is an example contract, not a universal schema. A physical artwork may specify substrate, circulation, size or duration instead of pixel fields. Document unsupported checks as unverified.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/handoff`>>
!! Handoff

Keep references in [[Reference Roles|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/reference-roles]]. Assess the outcome with [[Reception QA|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/reception-qa]]. Use [[Layer Composition|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/layer-composition]] where component operations require preservation and verification.

<<~/ahu>>

